Key Features: 
Batch Processing: Automatically detects and audits all PDF forms within the demo-files directory.
CI/CD Integrated: Powered by GitHub Actions; every "Push" triggers a fresh audit of all forms.
Dynamic Inputs: No hardcoded filenames. Simply drop a new .pdf into the demo folder, and the system scales to include it.
Artifact Traceability: Generates labeled audit results (audit-filename.pdf) stored as downloadable build artifacts.

🛠️ Technical Implementation
Language/Stack: Java 21, Maven, GitHub Actions.
Pattern: Uses Command Line Arguments (args[0]) to allow a shell loop in the YML to drive the Java logic.
Automation: The .github/workflows/main.yml handles the environment setup, build, and execution loop.

The Power of the Loop:
AuditPDF.java is designed to accept file paths as arguments. The Java code does not need to change when I add a new form, just update the data folder, and the GitHub Action loops through everything automatically.

The Build Pipeline (Actions):
By using GitHub Actions, we have a 'Source of Truth.' Anyone on the team can see the audit results in the 'Actions' tab under 'Artifacts' without even running the code locally.

## How to Run the Demo
1. **Local:** Run `mvn clean package` 
   Then: `java -jar target/GenerateTestPDF-1.0-SNAPSHOT.jar ./demo-files/your-file.pdf`
2. **GitHub:**
   Simply push any `.pdf` to the `/demo-files` folder. 
   Check the **Actions** tab to see the automated audit results.
